<title>USA: Koch Oil raises U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts.</title>
<headline>Koch Oil raises U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koch Oil said it raised the price it will  pay for U.S. crude oil by 25 cts a barrel, effective Friday.</p>
<p>The increase brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas  Intermediate to $18.25 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $15.50 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $17.75 and Oklahoma sweet is $18.25.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
